# Elixir with

## Section

`with(args)`: Combine matching clauses

Docs: [https://elixir.hexdocs.pm/Kernel.SpecialForms.html#with/1](https://elixir.hexdocs.pm/Kernel.SpecialForms.html#with/1)

One of the ways to understand `with` is to show which code patterns it improves. Imagine you have a map where the fields `width` and `height` are optional and you want to compute its area as `{:ok, area} or return `:error`.

<!-- livebook:{"break_markdown":true} -->

Implementing the function with `case`:

```elixir
defmodule Scratch do
  def area(opts) do
    case Map.fetch(opts, :width) do
      {:ok, width} ->
        case Map.fetch(opts, :height) do
          {:ok, height} -> {:ok, width * height}
          :error -> :error
        end
  
      :error ->
        :error
    end
  end
end

```

```elixir
opts = %{width: 17, height: 23}
Scratch.area(opts)
```

```elixir
opts = %{width: 17, h: 4}
Scratch.area(opts)
```

Implementing the function with `with`:

```elixir
defmodule ScratchTwo do
  def area(opts) do
    with {:ok, width} <- Map.fetch(opts, :width),
         {:ok, height} <- Map.fetch(opts, :height) do
      {:ok, width * height}
    end
  end
end
```

```elixir
opts = %{width: 12, height: 23}
ScratchTwo.area(opts)
```

```elixir
opts = %{w: 12, h: 22}
ScratchTwo.area(opts)
```
